a mother's grief heard across Iran after  the death of her daughter in police  custody in Tehran on September 16th  22 year old Masa amini was in the  capital with her brother visiting  relatives when she was detained by the  morality police three days earlier she  was accused of not properly wearing the  mandatory headscarf she was from  Kurdistan Province home to Iran's  Kurdish minority the police released the  security camera footage which they say  shows Masa arriving at a facility where  she was to go through what's called a  re-education class on the religious  benefits of wearing the headscar the  official autopsy report and subsequent  investigation launched by the government  alleged Massa had a pre-existing health  condition and suffered heart attack  while in police custody her family says  this is not true and accused the  morality police of beating her while in  custody  scenes like these followed her death and  sparked Nationwide protests driven by  women who demand an end to restrictive  dress rules in the country those who  backed the existing laws were allowed to  gather in Tehran to show their support  for the government while the president  was quick to address the issue in a live  televised interview  I told her family that this news was  shocking not just for me but for every  Iranian criticism and Dialogue on  various issues have a place in the  Constitution and can help us in the  decision-making process but the  distinction between protest and Riot  should be defined earlier this month  president raisi visited an all-female  University in Tehran where he praised  the movements of women in the field of  Academia simultaneously this was  happening outside the building where the  president was speaking  chanting Gracie get lost these  University students made their demands  clear  this Iranian MP warns without some  systematic reforms there could be  further consequences  it was due to the performance of the  system that she passed away they have to  express regret and apologize and revise  their methods the unrest that's followed  Masa amini's death has resulted in a  number of deaths including both  demonstrators and security officials  this is the area where Iran's morality  police arrested NASA amini on a Tuesday  afternoon since then they haven't been  seen much in the city whatever happens  next year regardless of which version of  events people believe it is clear that  masaamini's death has changed this  country  dorsa Jabari Al Jazeera Tehran
 

